  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(F(n)\\) is a function such that \\(F(1)=F(2)=F(3)=1,\\) and such that \\[ F(n+1)=\\frac{F(n)F(n-1)+1}{F(n-2)} \\] for \\(n\\ge3,\\) then \\(F(6)\\) is equal to:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(7\\)"
    },
    {
